---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="About Naman, the things he keeps building, and what usually sends him down a new rabbit hole.">
  <div class="shell shell--content page-intro">
    <h1>I usually build first and figure things out on the way.</h1>
    <p>
      I’m Naman. I like taking a small idea, making it real, and then finding ten ways it could be better.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="shell shell--content about-grid">
    <article class="prose about-copy">
      <p>
        That is basically how this site, Get Random Letter, and most of my experiments started. I’m not following some grand roadmap. I find something interesting or annoying, build a version, test it, improve it, and write down what I learned.
      </p>

      <h2 id="exploring">What I work on and keep exploring</h2>
      <p>
        SEO is part of my actual work: technical fixes, content, search data, and figuring out why a useful page isn’t getting found. I’m much more interested in using new tools to make something useful than arguing about which one won the week. WordPress still pulls me in too, because so much of the web runs on it—and there is plenty I’d like to make calmer and less annoying.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of what I write comes from work I’m doing right now, including the parts I’m still figuring out.
      </p>

      <h2 id="off-screen">When I’m off-screen</h2>
      <p>
        <em>One Piece</em> is the permanent favorite. I like stories with ridiculous ambition, weird crews, and a world that keeps getting bigger the farther you go. Chai also helps.
      </p>

      <h2>Why keep a personal site?</h2>
      <p>
        Because I don’t want everything I make to disappear into a feed. I want one place where a WordPress theme in beta can sit next to a weird wheel tool, an unfinished idea, and a post I still like six months later.
      </p>

      <h2>Colophon</h2>
      <p>
        I built Naman.blog with <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>, mostly plain CSS, and a tiny bit of JavaScript. <a href="https://pages.github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Pages<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> hosts it. The setup stays simple so I can spend more time making things than maintaining the site that lists them.
      </p>
    </article>

    <aside class="about-aside" aria-label="A few coordinates">
      <h2>A few coordinates</h2>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Making</dt><dd>Get Random Letter + Calm WP</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Working</dt><dd>SEO + search projects</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Writing</dt><dd>What I learn while doing it</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Recharging</dt><dd>One Piece + chai</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
